{"user": "a7 looks like it flips a ton along the bottom row diagonal - is that actually the strongest of my 3 options (g2, b6, a7) or is it a trap?", "user_ts": "2026-08-12T21:35:33.423982+00:00", "assistant": "**a7 is actually the strongest here, not a trap.**\n\nEven if it doesn\u2019t flip everything you first imagine, it matters because **a8 is already White\u2019s corner**, so a7 isn\u2019t handing over a new corner. It also takes important edge/diagonal discs and leaves White with fewer clean endgame choices than **g2** or **b6**.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-12T21:35:33.423982+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-12T21:35:38.423982+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Common Ground Question": 3, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Common Ground Question": 1.0, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification"], "consensus": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification"], "votes": {"Move Verdict": 3, "Local Justification": 3}, "confidence": {"Move Verdict": 1.0, "Local Justification": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification"], "llama": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification"], "sonnet": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Provide Correct Answer", "Direct Instruction"]}}
{"user": "Down to 4 empty squares. My choices are a1, g2, a3. Which one gives me the best final count?", "user_ts": "2026-08-12T21:35:48.423982+00:00", "assistant": "**Play a3.**\n\nEven though **a1 is a corner**, in this exact 4-empty endgame **a3** is strongest because it leaves White with **no legal move**, so White must pass and you get another move immediately. That tempo is worth more for the final count.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-12T21:35:48.423982+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-12T21:35:53.423982+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 2, "Common Ground Question": 2, "Solution Request": 1}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 0.6666666666666666, "Common Ground Question": 0.6666666666666666, "Solution Request": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"llama": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "gpt": ["Common Ground Question"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Solution Request"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification"], "consensus": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification"], "votes": {"Move Verdict": 3, "Local Justification": 3, "General Principle": 1, "Board Report": 1}, "confidence": {"Move Verdict": 1.0, "Local Justification": 1.0, "General Principle": 0.3333333333333333, "Board Report": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "llama": ["Move Verdict", "Board Report", "Local Justification"], "sonnet": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Provide Correct Answer", "Direct Instruction"]}}
{"user": "Looking back, I was least sure about that a3 move - why did it force White to pass with no legal moves at that point? I want to understand what made that square so strong.", "user_ts": "2026-08-12T21:36:03.423982+00:00", "assistant": "Because after **Black a3**, every remaining empty square failed White\u2019s legality test.\n\nFor White to have a move, an empty square must have a line like:\n\n**empty \u2192 black(s) \u2192 white**\n\nin some straight direction.\n\nAfter **a3**, the remaining empties did **not** give White any such line: the nearby black discs were either not bracketed by a White disc, or the line ran into another empty/edge. So White had **0 legal moves** and had to **pass**.\n\nThat\u2019s why **a3** was so strong: not because it flipped the most immediately, but because it won a **tempo** \u2014 you got to move again before White could reply. In a 4-empty endgame, that extra move often beats even taking a corner right away.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-12T21:36:03.423982+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-12T21:36:08.423982+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 2, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 0.6666666666666666, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "Local Justification": 3, "Worked Line": 1, "General Principle": 3, "Move Verdict": 1}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "Local Justification": 1.0, "Worked Li